        <body>
            <div xml:id="d304">

                <pb facs="0599" n="1253" sameAs="frus:frus1875v02/pg1253"/>

                <head>No. 596.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Cushing to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Marid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1875-04-21"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 21, 1875</date>.
                        (Received May 11.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 356.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In pursuance of the note addressed to me by
                    the minister of state in the afternoon of Friday the 16th instant, of which copy
                    is annexed <pb facs="0600" n="1254" xml:id="pg1254"/> to my No. 349, I called on
                    the minister of Hacienda the next day, Saturday the 17th, and he immediately
                    issued direction for the delivery of an order on the Bank of Spain for the sum
                    of 225,000 pesetas,($45,000,) which I received late on the same day, and
                    receipted for according to copy and translation annexed.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * *</p>
                <p>I have the honor, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>C. CUSHING.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d304-a1.xml" xpointer="d304-a1"/>
            </div>
